 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Types and gain grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The three types share every figure except voltage: BCX54 is rated 45 V collector-base and collector-emitter, BCX55 60 V for both, BCX56 100 V collector-base and 80 V collector-emitter. Without a suffix the gain spans 63 to 250; the -10 suffix narrows it to 63 to 160 and -16 to 100 to 250. Each of the nine parts carries a two-letter code on the body, for example BK for BCX56-10."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = 2 V the gain sits near 160 to 180 at 25 °C and near 225 to 240 at 100 °C from 1 mA to about 100 mA, then drops with rising current; the two curves meet near 100 at about 600 mA and fall to about 57 at 1 A (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "With collector current ten times the base current, VCE(sat) is about 28 mV at 1 mA, bottoms near 21 mV around 10 mA, and climbs to about 180 mV at 25 °C and 196 mV at 100 °C at 1 A (Fig.3). VBE(sat) under the same drive runs from about 0.58 V (25 °C) and 0.49 V (100 °C) at 1 mA to about 0.93 V and 0.87 V at 1 A (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 1 MHz the input capacitance Cib falls from about 120 pF at 0.1 V reverse bias to about 60 pF at 7 V, and the output capacitance Cob from about 22 pF at 0.1 V to about 5 pF at 20 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-89 body uses a molding compound rated UL 94V-0, is RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 to J-STD-020, with lead-free reflow peaking at 260 °C."
  }
 ],
